   "summary": "Rainfall in Central Java changed by about +56 mm/year per decade from 2001 to 2025 (Sen's slope). Along the trend line that is about +130 mm/year over the whole period. This trend is not statistically significant (Mann-Kendall p = 0.82). A trend can become significant with a longer record. The straight-line (OLS) t-test is not significant either.",
